import sys
sys.dont_write_bytecode=True
import additional_pfp_tests_remaining_audit as a
b='pfp/tests/'
assessments={
'test_code_change_checker_cli.py':'Full 133 lines. Temporary source-bound patch and configured binary SHA exercise canonical CLI diagnostics, three native calls and zero-call replay, protected-path failure, malformed source path/pin refusal before native dispatch, output no-overwrite and compatibility parser routing. The binary digest is computed from the currently located binary, so it binds the chosen executable but supplies no independent build/source provenance. Child environment removes only OPENROUTER_API_KEY and has no network sandbox. No binary discovery/read/execution or CLI run occurred in this audit.',
'test_code_change_repository_port.py':'Full 237 lines. Explicit in-memory test double observes lifecycle persistence schedule: patch on submit, three bound receipts after evaluation, run root only on finalize. Wrong patch bytes refuse before any evaluation artifact is stored while admitted patch remains. Tests document that persistence implementation, durability and atomic batch saving remain absent. Protocol surface test checks callable names, not signature/type conformance. Receipt identity and evidence hash length are useful structure checks, not semantic proof of code change. No controller or repository execution.',
'test_code_change_gates_stage.py':'Full 546 lines. Default controller path checks required gate ids/dispositions, refuses unsubmitted/cross-run/swapped-byte candidates at gates and finalize, propagates programming exceptions, keeps producer claim separate from actual disposition, binds packet/candidate/evaluator, reconstructs one ownership evidence digest, and distinguishes protected-inside-owned from ownership failure. All gates passing still yields DeclaredUnverified, with missing gates refused. Claim helper explicitly manufactures a public session ledger and labels that scaffolding/residual. The claimed evidence-change negative only compares three different gates on one candidate; per-gate constants can survive it (F101). No controller/native execution or semantic patch correctness established.',
'test_code_change_session_integrity.py':'Full 289 lines. Deriving task/payload from envelope blocks duplicate-field substitution; positive controls show wider policy changes packet identity. Malformed digest ledgers and unrelated fabricated memberships refuse. The source explicitly demonstrates public session reset and caller-supplied budget counters; these remain resource enforcement gaps, while unconditional BUDGET_HOST_STATE_ABSENT keeps the result DeclaredUnverified. It does not establish unforgeable admission. No source execution; documented residuals are not silently credited as closed.',
'test_code_change_submit_stage.py':'Full 312 lines. Canonical envelope/session lifecycle, packet identity sensitivity to objective, immutable updated ledger, different-patch candidate ids, exact full artifact payload/witness/metadata, byte-derived touched paths and absent producer claims are asserted. Sequential budget exhaustion and identical resubmission without spending are tested. This is consistency under caller-carried session state, subject to the reset residual in the sibling integrity tests; no authenticated/durable budget or semantic correctness of generated code. No controller/parser/native execution.',
'test_diff_parser_multifile.py':'Full 231 lines. Meaningful positive and negative twins isolate plain multi-file parsing, git header disagreement, nonempty honest refusal messages, and leading/trailing header-only sections. Refused patches must expose no touched paths; malformed fixtures are asserted invalid to avoid vacuity. Two/three/five files are bounded examples despite any-count wording. Parsing touched paths is syntactic patch structure, not applicability to a base tree, allowed path policy or correctness of changed program. No original parser execution.'}
for name,s in assessments.items():a.record(b+name,1,len(a.source(b+name)),s)
n=a.read('_notes.json');ev=lambda name,x,y:{'path':b+name,'sha256':a.row(b+name)['sha256'],'lines':[x,y]}
n['findings'].append({'id':'PFPTESTS-F101','severity':'low','statement':'The gate evidence-change test compares different gates rather than changing one gate input.','evidence':[ev('test_code_change_gates_stage.py',361,392)],'reason':'The first test recomputes ownership evidence on one fixture; the second requires three gate digests to differ on that same fixture. A mutant returning one fixed digest per gate, with the ownership constant set to this fixture digest, passes both. A same-gate altered-input comparison is needed to test the claimed dependency.','limits':'Static mutation argument limited to these two assertions; no production hash-binding failure claimed.'})
n['claims'].append({'id':'PFPTESTS-CL035','statement':'Code-change tests preserve a useful distinction between self-consistent candidate/patch admission and trustworthy host history: public sessions and caller budget counters remain resettable, and their positive gates intentionally terminate as DeclaredUnverified.','evidence':[ev('test_code_change_gates_stage.py',244,268),ev('test_code_change_gates_stage.py',440,478),ev('test_code_change_session_integrity.py',217,289),ev('test_code_change_repository_port.py',194,209)],'limits':'Source-level controls and explicitly documented residuals; no fresh native or application execution, durable repository implementation or proof of patch semantics.'})
a.write('_notes.json',n);a.report()
